{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And kept My charge.</b> A general term encompassing everything he is obligated to keep of commandments, statutes, and teachings. It is possible that the commandment is \"Go forth\" (Genesis 12:1), and also \"Take now your son\" (Genesis 22:2)." "<b>And My statutes.</b> They are the statutes of HaShem, that a person should walk after His deeds, as I will explain in the verse שעטנז (Leviticus 19:19), and these statutes are implanted in the heart, and the Torah is that he circumcised himself, his sons, and his servants, and in the verse \"and the Torah and the commandment\" (Exodus 24:12) I will explain them well."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "Genesis 22:2 citation given in the Hebrew as כ\"ב; resolved to 2.", 1 "The referent of \"the Torah\" is left syntactically ambiguous in the source; translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:53.163181870Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}